        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many years do these fixes hold up?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Gutter and grading fixes last as long as you maintain them. Polyurethane crack injections often last decades. Masonry coatings typically go five to ten years before touch-ups. Interior drain systems can last many decades, though sump pumps usually need replacing every 7 to 10 years. Exterior membranes, installed well, are often expected to last as long as the foundation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a permit to waterproof my basement?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Gutter work, grading, crack sealing and coatings usually do not need a permit. Interior drain installation, sump pump discharge lines and excavation sometimes do, depending on your municipality, especially if discharge connects to a storm sewer or crosses a property line. Check with your local building department, and ask any contractor whether they pull permits."
          }
