            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Treat it as serious if water pools on the floor after storms, if a crack is horizontal or wider than about a quarter inch, if a wall bows inward, or if the leak is growing season to season. Damp spots, light efflorescence and condensation are lower priority. When structure is in question, a structural engineer is a better first call than a waterproofing salesperson."
